# Single Google Cloud API key, used by the frontend (3D tiles, Routes,
# Places autocomplete, Geocoding, Weather) and the Solar API proxy at
# server/index.js.
#
# Enable each of these on the project in the Google Cloud console — the
# app degrades visibly when any one is missing, and surfaces a console
# warning naming the API:
#
#   1. Map Tiles API (Photorealistic 3D Tiles)
#        https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/tile.googleapis.com
#   2. Routes API
#        https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/routes.googleapis.com
#   3. Places API (for the autocomplete in SearchBar)
#        https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/places.googleapis.com
#   4. Geocoding API (for reverse-geocoding origin auto-fill — without
#      this the app falls back to OpenStreetMap Nominatim)
#        https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/geocoding-backend.googleapis.com
#   5. Weather API (for wind direction/speed, cloud, precipitation)
#        https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/weather.googleapis.com
#   6. Solar API (for per-building annual sunshine data — proxied
#      server-side via /api/solar so the key never reaches the browser
#      for this call)
#        https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/solar.googleapis.com
#
# Also set a billing budget alert (Solar + Routes are the main cost
# drivers; per-day quota caps recommended in dev).
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Google Generative Language API key for Gemini 2.5 Flash — drives the
# conversational routing input in the route sheet (src/lib/geminiRouting.ts).
# Called directly from the browser using JSON-mode + responseSchema, so
# AI Studio credits cover it without a proxy. Without the key, the
# conversational input is disabled (the filter pills still work).
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=
